lib/
stan-cache/
.bayesnec-src/
hpc/local.conf
*.sif
*.log
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# The individual unit fits: 189 of them, and the assembled store beside them is
# what the render reads. Kept on the cluster and fetched with hpc/fetch-store.sh
# rather than tracked.
units/

# The store: nine model-averaged fits, a few hundred megabytes. Reproducible
# from this code, manifest.rds and hpc/bayesnec.lock, so what tracking it would
# save is the fitting rather than the record. The index and the provenance stamp
# beside it are small and are tracked.
store/*.rds

# The post-fit results hpc/run.post writes beside them: hundreds of files, some
# the size of a model set. The task list, logs and MANIFEST in store/post/ are
# small and are tracked.
store/post/*.rds
store/post/*.part*

# Rebuilt by hpc/run.install against the deployed vignette, so a copy committed
# from a workstation would be a fourth thing that can drift from the render.
# manifest.csv is tracked as the readable record of the 189 units; the .rds it
# is written beside is not.
manifest.rds
